1. Statistical Edge in Noisy Markets
Top quantitative trading firms like Two Sigma, Renaissance Technologies, and Jump Trading don't rely on single models because financial markets (especially crypto) are extremely noisy environments. In these markets:
Single models inevitably capture spurious correlations
Market regimes change frequently, making any single approach unreliable
Signal-to-noise ratio is incredibly low (often <5% signal)
What top firms do: They deploy dozens or hundreds of weakly predictive models that, when combined properly, create robust predictions. This approach reduces the variance in their forecasts while maintaining or increasing predictive power - a fundamental advantage your system currently lacks.
